  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Aircraft Manufacturing (NAICS 336411) shows $39.1B in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer with $38.5B of obligations, leaving other agencies to account for the remainder. Award activity totals 4,887 contracts with an average award size of $8M. Obligations are down 36.2% year over year, and FY2026 to date sits below FY25 and FY23 totals while close to FY21 and FY22 levels. Lockheed Martin Corporation leads vendors with $11.3B in obligations, followed by several Boeing entries that together represent multiple large awards across the top vendor list. The market is concentrated by buyer and vendor: one agency accounts for the vast majority of obligations and a handful of prime contractors account for the largest shares. All figures are contract obligations and current-year totals are partial, fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What is the size and recent trend of the Aircraft Manufacturing federal market?",
